{{also|Sinus|sinüs}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=sinus}}

===Etymology===
{{ubor|en|la|sinus||a bent surface, curve, hollow}}. {{doublet|en|sine}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsaɪ.nəs/}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪnəs}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy|zootomy}} A [[pouch]] or [[cavity]] in a [[bone]] or other [[tissue]], especially one in the bones of the [[face]] or [[skull]] connecting with the [[nasal cavity|nasal cavities]] {{gl|the [[paranasal sinus]]}}.
#: {{hypo|en|ethmoid sinus|frontal sinus|maxillary sinus|paranasal sinus|piriform sinus|Rokitansky-Aschoff sinus|sphenoid sinus}}
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} An [[irregular]] [[venous]] or [[lymphatic]] [[cavity]], [[reservoir]], or [[dilated]] [[vessel]].
#: {{hypo|en|carotid sinus|cavernous sinus|coronary sinus|petrosal sinus|sagittal sinus|venous sinus}}
## {{lb|en|physiology|attributive}} Relating to or denoting the [[sinoatrial node]] of the [[heart]] or its function of [[regulate|regulating]] the [[heartbeat]].
# {{lb|en|pathology}} An [[abnormal]] [[cavity]] or [[passage]] such as a [[fistula]], leading from a [[deep-seated]] [[infection]] and [[discharge|discharging]] [[pus]] to the surface.
# {{lb|en|botany}} A [[rounded]] [[notch]] or [[depression]] between two [[lobe]]s or [[tooth|teeth]] in the [[margin]] of a [[leaf]] or [[petal]].
# {{lb|en|geography}} A [[bay]] of the [[sea]]; a [[recess]] in the [[shore]].

